Available Commands:
  authorize-evm-delegation Consent, with your post-quantum key, to one EIP-7702 delegation of your account
  clear-evm-delegation     Remove your account's EIP-7702 delegation, with your post-quantum key
  close-evm-window         Revoke your EVM-lane authorisation window immediately
  close-svm-window         Revoke your SVM-lane authorisation window immediately
  cosign                   PQC+classical sign a generate-only tx and broadcast it (or print it, or estimate its gas)
  gen-kem-key              Generate and store an ML-KEM-1024 key pair for receiving encrypted data
  gen-key                  Generate and store a Dilithium-5 key for client-side hybrid signing
  migrate-key              Migrate your PQC key to a new algorithm (dual-signature required)
  multisig-assemble        Assemble the classical member signatures and broadcast (or print) the multisig transaction
  multisig-classical-sign  Sign a combined multisig transaction as one classical member (SIGN_MODE_DIRECT)
  multisig-combine         Combine post-quantum member signatures into the transaction's multisig extension
  multisig-member-proof    Prove, as a post-quantum member, that you hold your key and consent to the multisig (offline)
  multisig-register        Register (or re-register) the post-quantum member set of a multisig account
  multisig-sign            Sign a multisig transaction as one post-quantum member (offline with --offline)
  open-evm-window          Authorise your EVM lane for a bounded number of blocks, transactions and value
  open-svm-window          Authorise a Solana wallet key for your account, bounded in blocks, transactions and value
  recover-key              Recover a Dilithium-5 key deterministically from a mnemonic (read from stdin)
  register-kem-key         Publish your ML-KEM encryption public key so others can encrypt to your account
  register-key             Register a PQC key for your account (legacy, defaults to Dilithium-5)
  register-key-v2          Register a PQC key with explicit algorithm selection (v0.6.0)
  remove-kem-key           Withdraw your published ML-KEM encryption public key
  rotate-key               Rotate your ML-DSA-87 key to a new key of the same algorithm (mnemonic on stdin)

